k you'll have to  submit it for clinical trials or  anything like that the FDA's regulations  that that are that are likely to come  out before the end of this year are  going to be under their authority under  the Center for tobacco products and the  center for tobacco products has  jurisdiction over tobacco products and  products derived from tobacco under this  2009 Family Smoking Prevention and  Tobacco Control Act and it's different  from their drug jurisdiction their  authorities more limited under the  center for tobacco products so what we  expect to see are regulations like  ingredient disclosures Good  Manufacturing Practices age verification  things that will prevent youth access to  the product what about more of the local  legislation the ban saying you can't  vape indoors when the government made  the decision to ban indoor tobacco  smoking that was based on very real  rigorous scientific testing and data  that showed that secondhand smoke was  harmful  well there's no evidence to support that  the exhaled vapor mist is harmful and  and in fact some of the increasing  published peer-reviewed scientific  research is showing that it certainly  doesn't have anything close to the harm  potential of tobacco cigarettes and it's  not clear to me whether whether it has  any any harm whatsoever  and so our policy makers in government  should be making all of their decisions  based on science and data and so not on  conjecture not on well if it looks like  a cigarette it must be cigarette that  that's not data that's not science and  that's not how we should be making  decisions do you think that if your  product didn't look like a cigarette  they wouldn't be as much skepticism part  of it I think is a combination that it  does look like a cigarette creates some  of that confusion part of its also  unfortunately I didn't choose the name  electronic cigarette but it's got the  word cigarette in it and it's very hard  to unring that Bell and sometimes I say  you know our products as much a  cigarette is a car and electric horse  you know but but unfortunately it's it's  got that name I mean we have no tobacco  in our product we have no come we don't  combust we're not burning anything we're  not lighting anything on fire and while  it might look like a cigarette inside is  an integrated circuit ship lithium ion  battery a heating element a fairly  sophisticated chemistry there's there's  a lot going on in a fairly small package  so do you think it's ironic that for a  country that's been trying to eradicate  traditional cigarettes for so long that  they there's been a little bit of  backlash against a product that's  supposed to be helping with that yeah I  mean it's very interested it's a very  interesting situation that the  government and public health has spent  billions of dollars for decades to try  to stem the tide of this public health  epidemic and yet despite all of these  resources that have been spent by the  government they really haven't made a  really serious dent in the last 10 years  in the number of people who smoke in  this country and what I think is amazing  about what a company like njoy is doing  is we're using technology and and that's  what we do in America we use technology  to solve really complicated problems and  so we're using technology to address  this really systemic problem this public  health epidemic in the sense that if you  look again back at the data  the number of people the number of  people smoking has been decreasing as  the popularity of electronic cigarettes  has been increasing great well Craig  thank you so much it's my pleasure thank  you for even TV I'm Tracy Oppenheimer  [Music]

